# cw-tune-default: the CW page of the button bar with the CW tune widget and the
# radio in the state the issue #122 reports ("the Tune widget does not appear on
# the CW band"): nothing is touched, the Tuner parameter is at its boot value.
#
# The route is the user's: the KEY key loads the key pages (src/main_screen.c,
# KEYPAD_KEY -> buttons_load_page_group(buttons_group_key)) and the page button
# cycles to `page_cw_decoder_1` (src/buttons.cpp), the "(CW 1:2)" page that holds
# Decoder / Tuner / Dec SN R. The rig is in CW and cw_tune is at its boot value
# (0, the port default, src/cfg/cfg.c:349) with the button reading Off: what the
# fixture *means* is that the widget shows anyway, because the visibility rule is
# the mode (CW/CWR) and no longer the parameter. scenario_settle codifies exactly
# that (the "(CW 1:2)" page, the "Tuner" button reading Off, cw_tune still 0, the
# widget not hidden, and cw_tune_ui_visible() agreeing with it), so the capture is
# the state of the issue *after* the fix and not a different page.
#
# The theme is the radio's own (Redshift), so the render matches the user's screen.

name cw-tune-default
screen cw-tune-default

theme Redshift
seed 20

frequency_hz 7030000
tx_frequency_hz 7030000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode cw
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
